      "revision": 106370490,
      "text": "ノミノツヅリ(小無心菜)は、ごく小型のナデシコ科の雑草。道ばたで見かけることが多い。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Arenaria serpyllifolia」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arenaria_serpyllifolia",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1350208604,
      "text": "Arenaria serpyllifolia, commonly known as thyme-leaf sandwort or thyme-leaved sandwort, is an annual or biennial flowering plant in the pink and carnation family Caryophyllaceae that can be found from Nepal to Pakistan. It also has a wide distribution in the United Kingdom and southern Poland. It was introduced to Chile. The species is widespread in China."
    }
